      "README.md": "# O(1) LRU and Frequency-Bucketed LFU Cache Engine\n\n## Overview\n\nStrict O(1) LRU and Shah-Mitra-Matani frequency-bucketed LFU caches built over sentinel-guarded intrusive doubly linked lists with zero heap-log overhead.\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: Sentinel-Guarded Intrusive Doubly Linked List\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Eliminating Null Checks with Dummy Head and Tail Sentinels\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`DoublyLinkedList.addFront / DoublyLinkedList.remove`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `addFront(node)` and `remove(node)` on `DoublyLinkedList`. Because `this.head` and `this.tail` are permanent dummy sentinel nodes, every real node always has non-null `node.prev` and `node.next`. `addFront` splices `node` between `head` and `head.next`; `remove` links `node.prev.next = node.next` and `node.next.prev = node.prev`.\n- **Verification Invariant**: splices and unlinks nodes in O(1) using sentinel head and tail\n\n### Step 2: O(1) LRU Cache via Hash Map + Recency List\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Composing Hash Lookups with Intrusive List Promotion\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`LRUCache.get / LRUCache.put`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `get(key)` and `put(key, value)` on `LRUCache`. - Most recently used node sits at `list.head.next`; least recently used sits at `list.tail.prev`. - On `get(key)`: unlink node and `addFront(node)`. - On `put(key, value)`: if `map.size === capacity`, evict `list.popBack()` and delete its key from `map`.\n- **Verification Invariant**: evicts least-recently-used key in O(1) time\n\n### Step 3: Frequency Bucket Promotion & minFreq Invariant\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Shah-Mitra-Matani O(1) Frequency Bucket Advancement\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`LFUCache._promote`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `_promote(node)` on `LFUCache`. When `node` moves from `oldFreq` to `oldFreq + 1`, remove it from `buckets.get(oldFreq)`. If that bucket becomes empty **and** `this.minFreq === oldFreq`, increment `this.minFreq = oldFreq + 1`. Then insert `node` at the front of `buckets.get(oldFreq + 1)`.\n- **Verification Invariant**: advances minFreq exactly when the minimum frequency bucket empties\n\n### Step 4: LFU Insertion & Tie-Breaking LRU Eviction\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Evicting Tail of buckets[minFreq] & Resetting minFreq = 1\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`LFUCache.put`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `put(key, value)` on `LFUCache`. 1. If `key` exists, update `node.value = value` and call `this._promote(node)`. 2. If at capacity, pop the LRU victim from `this.buckets.get(this.minFreq).popBack()` and delete it from `this.nodes`. 3. Insert the new node into bucket `1` and set `this.minFreq = 1`.\n- **Verification Invariant**: evicts lowest-frequency key and breaks ties by least-recently-used order\n\n## Asymptotic & Memory Layout Guarantees\n\n- **Category**: Linked Structures & Caching\n- **Difficulty**: Advanced (~35 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - Sentinel-guarded doubly linked list eliminating null-pointer branches\n  - Shah-Mitra-Matani O(1) LFU cache with frequency-bucketed LRU tie-breaking\n  - Exact minFreq invariant maintenance across hits, promotions, and evictions\n- **Tags & Primitives**: `LFU Cache`, `LRU Cache`, `Intrusive Linked List`, `O(1) Eviction`, `Frequency Buckets`\n\n## Production Systems Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch implementation is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal invariant—from pointer restoration and bitmask addressing to amortized potential bounds and tree height balance—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n\n"
