      "README.md": "# Open-Addressing Robin Hood Hash Map with Backward-Shift Deletion\n\n## Overview\n\nAn open-addressed hash table implementing Celis Robin Hood displacement, early-exit lookups on PSL ordering, and tombstone-free backward-shift deletion.\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: Probe Sequence Length (PSL) Arithmetic on Power-of-2 Ring\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Measuring Cyclic Probe Distance via Bitmask Subtraction\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RobinHoodHashMap._psl`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `_psl(slotIdx, idealIdx)` to compute how many linear probes an entry at `slotIdx` has traveled from `idealIdx`. In a power-of-two table, `(slotIdx - idealIdx) & this._mask` handles wrap-around across index `0` in $O(1)$ without branches.\n- **Verification Invariant**: computes cyclic probe sequence length across wrap-around\n\n### Step 2: Robin Hood Displacement Insertion\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Stealing Slots from \"Rich\" Keys (Small PSL) to Give to \"Poor\" Keys (Large PSL)\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RobinHoodHashMap.set`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `set(key, value)` with Robin Hood swap semantics. 1. If `(this._size + 1) > this._capacity * this._maxLoad`, double capacity via `this._resize(this._capacity * 2)`. 2. Walk linearly from `idx = this._idealIndex(key)`. If `cur.key === entry.key`, overwrite `cur.value`. 3. If `entry.psl > cur.psl`, swap `entry` and `this._slots[idx]` and continue probing with the displaced entry.\n- **Verification Invariant**: inserts keys and bounds PSL variance via Robin Hood displacement\n\n### Step 3: Early-Exit Lookup on PSL Monotonicity\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Aborting Unsuccessful Searches When currentPSL > occupantPSL\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RobinHoodHashMap.get`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `get(key)` with early termination. Because Robin Hood insertion guarantees that any key with a larger `psl` would have displaced an occupant with a smaller `cur.psl`, if `cur === null || psl > cur.psl`, the target key cannot exist further down the probe chain.\n- **Verification Invariant**: terminates lookups early when probe distance exceeds occupant PSL\n\n### Step 4: Tombstone-Free Backward-Shift Deletion\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Healing Probe Chains by Shifting Displaced Neighbors Left\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RobinHoodHashMap.delete`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `delete(key)` using backward-shift deletion instead of tombstones. 1. Locate `key` at `idx` (returning `false` if absent). 2. Clear `this._slots[idx] = null` and decrement `this._size`. 3. While `next = (prev + 1) & _mask` is occupied and `this._slots[next].psl > 0`, shift `this._slots[next]` into `prev`, decrement its `psl`, and advance.\n- **Verification Invariant**: deletes keys via backward-shift without leaving tombstones\n\n## Asymptotic & Memory Layout Guarantees\n\n- **Category**: Hashing & Sketches\n- **Difficulty**: Advanced (~35 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - Probe Sequence Length (PSL) displacement minimizing probe variance\n  - Early-exit search termination when current PSL exceeds occupant PSL\n  - Tombstone-free backward-shift deletion preventing probe degradation\n- **Tags & Primitives**: `Robin Hood Hashing`, `Open Addressing`, `Backward-Shift Delete`, `PSL Variance`, `FNV-1a`\n\n## Production Systems Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch implementation is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal invariant—from pointer restoration and bitmask addressing to amortized potential bounds and tree height balance—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n\n"
