      "README.md": "# Left-Leaning Red-Black Order-Statistic Tree\n\n## Architecture & 2-3 Tree Isomorphism\n\nStandard Red-Black trees require separate left/right cases across multiple insertion and deletion fixup patterns. Robert Sedgewick's **Left-Leaning Red-Black (LLRB)** tree establishes a strict 1-to-1 bijection with **2-3 trees** by enforcing that all red links lean left:\n\n1. **No node has a red right child** (`isRed(h.right) === false`).\n2. **No node has two consecutive left red links** (`isRed(h.left) && isRed(h.left.left) === false`).\n3. **Perfect black balance**: every path from the root to a `null` link traverses the exact same number of black links.\n\nBecause of this invariant, bottom-up insertion cleanup collapses into just three conditional statements in `_fixUp(h)`:\n\n```js\nif (this._isRed(h.right) && !this._isRed(h.left)) h = this._rotateLeft(h);\nif (this._isRed(h.left) && this._isRed(h.left.left)) h = this._rotateRight(h);\nif (this._isRed(h.left) && this._isRed(h.right)) this._flipColors(h);\n```\n\n## Subtree Size Augmentation for Order Statistics\n\nBy storing `node.size = 1 + size(node.left) + size(node.right)` in every node and updating it in $O(1)$ during rotations, our balanced BST becomes an **Order-Statistic Tree**:\n\n- `select(k)`: Returns the $k$-th smallest key ($0 \\le k < n$) in $O(\\log n)$ time by comparing $k$ against `leftSize = size(curr.left)`.\n- `rank(key)`: Returns the count of keys strictly less than `key` in $O(\\log n)$ time by accumulating `1 + size(curr.left)` whenever descending right.\n- `rangeCount(lo, hi)`: Computes the exact number of elements in $[\\text{lo}, \\text{hi}]$ in $O(\\log n)$ time via `rank(hi) - rank(lo) + (has(hi) ? 1 : 0)`.\n\n## Deletion via Red-Link Pushing\n\nDeletion in a 2-3 tree is trivial if we never land on a 2-node at a leaf. On the way down the tree, `_moveRedLeft` and `_moveRedRight` borrow from a sibling or merge across the parent so that the current search node always carries a red link, guaranteeing $O(\\log n)$ worst-case deletion.\n\n## Curriculum Connections\n\n- [Red-Black Trees & Left-Leaning RB (LLRB)](#topic/red-black-llrb-isomorphism)\n- [AVL Trees & Rotation Mechanics](#topic/tree-rotations-avl-invariants)\n- [BST Augmentation & Order-Statistic Trees](#topic/augmented-trees-order-intervals)\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: Rotations, Color Flips & Size Maintenance\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Rotations, Color Flips & Size Maintenance\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`Step1`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `_rotateLeft(h)`, `_rotateRight(h)`, and `_flipColors(h)`. Whenever links rotate, preserve the parent link color (`x.color = h.color; h.color = RED`) and recompute subtree sizes bottom-up.\n- **Verification Invariant**: verifies Step 1: Rotations, Color Flips & Size Maintenance\n\n### Step 2: LLRB Insertion & 3-Line FixUp\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: LLRB Insertion & 3-Line FixUp\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`Step2`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `_put(h, key, value)` and `_fixUp(h)`. Every 2-3 tree insertion maps to 3 local rules on the return path: rotate right-leaning red links left, rotate consecutive left-leaning red links right, and flip colors when both children are red.\n- **Verification Invariant**: verifies Step 2: LLRB Insertion & 3-Line FixUp\n\n### Step 3: Order Statistics (rank & select)\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Order Statistics (rank & select)\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`Step3`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Use the `node.size` augmentation to implement `rank(key)` (number of keys `< key`) and `select(k)` (the 0-indexed $k$-th smallest key) in $O(\\log n)$ time.\n- **Verification Invariant**: verifies Step 3: Order Statistics (rank & select)\n\n### Step 4: Top-Down 2-3-4 Deletion with Red-Link Pushing\n\n- **Core Mechanical Concept**: Top-Down 2-3-4 Deletion with Red-Link Pushing\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`Step4`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `delete(key)` using Sedgewick's `_moveRedLeft` and `_moveRedRight` helpers so the current node is never a 2-node on the descent path, followed by `_fixUp` on ascent.\n- **Verification Invariant**: verifies Step 4: Top-Down 2-3-4 Deletion with Red-Link Pushing\n\n## Asymptotic & Memory Layout Guarantees\n\n- **Category**: Balanced Trees & Augmentation\n- **Difficulty**: Advanced (~50 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - Sedgewick Left-Leaning Red-Black (LLRB) 2-3 tree isomorphism with 3 local fixup operations\n  - Subtree size augmentation maintained across rotateLeft, rotateRight, and moveRedLeft/Right\n  - O(log n) order-statistic queries: rank(key), select(k), and rangeCount(lo, hi)\n- **Tags & Primitives**: `LLRB Tree`, `2-3 Tree Isomorphism`, `Order Statistics`, `Tree Rotations`, `Rank & Select`\n\n## Production Systems Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch implementation is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal invariant—from pointer restoration and bitmask addressing to amortized potential bounds and tree height balance—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n\n"
